WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.320
Most Americans agree on one thing — gun

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.799
violence

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.560
is a problem. According to one survey

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:42.799
it's a pretty huge majority

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.079
with only 6% who say it's not a

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:45.840
problem at all.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:47.840
The question of how to tackle gun

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.840
violence is where there's debate

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.399
and at the heart of that debate is gun

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.880
control and whether more laws are needed.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:56.320
But before we get into that let's debunk

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.680
the myth that gun control

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:02.159
is anything new. 

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.599
In the 1930s they banned machine guns in

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.599
response to gangs.

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:29.760
In the late '60s after the assassination

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:32.000
of President JFK

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.160
the Gun Control Act came in. It imposed

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.840
regulations on the firearms industry

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.920
and came up with a list of people who

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.160
could be denied the sale of guns.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.319
And in the '90s President Clinton's Crime

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.800
Bill introduced a federal ban on assault

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.400
weapons but that expired 10 years later.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:52.319
And that goes back to the constitution.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.200
For Americans

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:57.120
being able to own a gun is a basic right

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.959
up there with free speech.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.280
The Second Amendment says "a

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:03.599
well-regulated militia, being necessary

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.920
to the security of a free state,

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.080
the right of the people to keep and bear

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.159
arms, shall not be infringed."

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.760
So what does that mean? Well, for a couple

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:14.319
of hundred years the understanding

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.080
focused on that mention of a militia.

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:17.360
It's really the idea that the states

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.920
would serve as a check

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.440
against a possible tyrannical government.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.280
Makes sense seeing as it was written

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.159
after the War of Independence.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.560
And that idea still persists today but

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:30.319
in 2008 there was a landmark Supreme

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.519
Court decision that focused on the

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:33.920
second half.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:35.840
It's known as the Heller case. The court

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.239
ruled that a ban on handguns in the

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.480
district of Columbia was

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:40.080
unconstitutional

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.560
and for the first time affirmed the

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.440
right for individuals to keep arms for

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.680
self-defence

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.680
in the home. 

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.720
And that shift in thinking among

00:03:56.959 --> 00:04:02.640
Americans started happening

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:04.720
well before 2008. 

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.320
The National Rifle

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.479
Association —

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.560
the US's main gun rights advocacy group —

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:38.960
has also played a big part in that.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.160
In pushing the idea that guns are needed

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.440
for self-defence.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.600
We can't get away from the fact that

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:15.840
this is all super political

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.120
and we see that when it comes to support

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.120
for gun laws.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.400
Overall more than half of Americans

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.240
favour stricter laws

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.400
but when you break that down more than

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:25.840
80% of Democrats support more gun

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:28.320
control compared to just

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.919
20% of Republicans. 

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.680
So what do US gun laws look like?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.360
Well, that depends on where you live.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.880
There are federal laws that apply

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.039
across the whole country that for

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.360
instance ban convicted felons, people

00:05:55.039 --> 00:05:57.919
with

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.280
mental illness or kids under 18 from

00:05:57.919 --> 00:06:01.280
buying guns.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.360
But then there are state laws and each

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.960
state has a lot of leeway to enforce

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:07.520
their own regulations

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.960
and they differ pretty wildly. 

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:20.479
In Massachusetts, a

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.000
strongly Democratic state,

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.840
you need a police permit and a

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.840
background check to buy a gun.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.840
While Republican-controlled Texas

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.080
recently passed a law allowing people to

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.880
carry concealed handguns without any

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.919
permit.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.960
So now we've got a Democrat in the White

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.680
House and President Biden has declared

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.680
gun violence a public health epidemic.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:52.000
His plans to tackle it include more

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.319
money for community programmes to address

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.680
some of the root causes of gun violence.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.240
On the legal side Biden wants to toughen

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.840
up gun laws

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.000
and make sure the ones that already

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.400
exist are actually applied —

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.919
including zero tolerance for rogue gun

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.599
dealers. 

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:41.440
He also wants to tighten the rules

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:41.440
on what are called ghost guns.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.520
These are weapons sold in parts and

00:07:43.599 --> 00:07:46.160
without a serial number so they can't be

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.360
traced.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.039
Another big thing Biden wants to

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.840
do

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:11.360
is bring back the ban on assault weapons.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:13.520
Guns like the semi-automatic AR-15 rifle.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.520
According to a Newsweek investigation

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.720
this type of gun was used in more than a

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.120
quarter of the last

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.879
80 mass shootings. Like this year's

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.000
attack in a supermarket in Boulder,

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:24.879
Colorado,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.960
the Orlando nightclub shooting in 2016

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:29.120
and at Sandy Hook Elementary School,

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.400
where 20 children and six teachers were

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.360
killed in 2012.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:35.200
But can he do it? As Democrats push for

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.760
more gun control there are plenty of

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.560
voters

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:40.000
and politicians in Congress who say guns

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.680
just aren't the problem.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.640
Now even though we always hear about how

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.720
America is so divided over guns

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:13.680
there's another way to look at it. 

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.680
Guns aren't going away — that's a

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.920
non-starter in the US.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.680
But if Americans can find that common

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:44.640
ground to look at policies they can

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.399
agree on

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:51.200
maybe that's where there's a chance of

00:09:46.399 --> 00:09:53.200
saving lives.

